# g3x-policy-native -> lead (native/mixdog-window is its own workspace with its own Cargo.lock)
1. native/mixdog-window/Cargo.lock: the new path dependency mixdog-browser-policy (../core/crates/mixdog-browser-policy) adds it and its
   crates (mixdog-js, mixdog-workspace-hack, regress, icu_collator, icu_locale_core, sys-locale, chrono, chrono-tz, iana-time-zone, serde,
   serde_json, async-trait, tokio, url and their dependencies) to the lock. build.ps1 runs `cargo build --locked`, so regenerate it once,
   offline, from the versions already in native/core/Cargo.lock (cargo update -w --offline in native/mixdog-window, or copy the matching
   package entries) before the first build; I did not run cargo.
2. Weight / crt-static: the crate's only async parts are url_admission.rs (async-trait, tokio "sync"); the module does not call them. If the
   .node grows too much or tokio refuses +crt-static, the smallest split is a default-on feature `admission` in mixdog-browser-policy that
   gates `pub mod url_admission`, async-trait and tokio, and `default-features = false` on the dependency line in
   native/mixdog-window/Cargo.toml. Not needed otherwise.
3. Tests: every desktop test that imports a browser module (url-policy / redaction importers: agent-bridge, host-policy, restore-pages, ...)
   now loads mixdog_window.node at import and stops with a named error when it is absent: build it before the desktop test run.
